1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,460
Fourteen WebMCP tools live on this page.

2
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:06,563
With nothing open, three of them exist.

3
00:00:06,700 --> 00:00:09,760
Open a document and two more appear.

4
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:15,015
It asks what it is looking at, and gets a shape.

5
00:00:15,100 --> 00:00:18,160
Types, pages, counts — never the text.

6
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:21,290
The detector runs here, on this device.

7
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:23,110
Nothing is uploaded.

8
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:26,163
Fifty-six confidential values, found in seconds.

9
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:29,450
This is everything the agent receives back.

10
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:33,336
Type, page, confidence — and the value blocked out.

11
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:38,250
It is redacting a document it is not allowed to
read.

12
00:00:38,300 --> 00:00:41,810
When it needs a real value, it has to ask.

13
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:45,363
It is waiting for me right now.

14
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:49,830
I read the reason, and release the sender's name.

15
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:54,418
Consent needs a screen, and a human in front of it.

16
00:00:54,500 --> 00:00:56,493
This one I refuse.

17
00:00:56,600 --> 00:01:00,242
Refusal comes back as an answer, not an error.

18
00:01:00,400 --> 00:01:04,430
That is why this is WebMCP, and not a server.

19
00:01:04,600 --> 00:01:07,150
One sentence of policy.

20
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:10,066
Thirty-one values matched across two pages.

21
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:15,500
I see the plan drawn on the document before anything
is touched.

22
00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:19,120
The highlighted spans are what will disappear.

23
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:21,784
The amounts stay.

24
00:01:22,400 --> 00:01:23,850
Apply is irreversible.

25
00:01:23,900 --> 00:01:28,415
It tells me how many values go, and how many stay.

26
00:01:28,500 --> 00:01:30,493
The approval is mine.

27
00:01:30,800 --> 00:01:33,472
And nothing is drawn over anything.

28
00:01:33,600 --> 00:01:39,764
The characters are removed from the file, and the
rectangle is drawn where they were.

29
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:46,855
Then it proves it, against the bytes of the export
rather than what the screen draws.

30
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:49,330
Thirty-one values checked.

31
00:01:49,600 --> 00:01:52,369
Nothing under the rectangle to find.

32
00:01:52,500 --> 00:01:55,560
Export needs a click as well.

33
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:58,380
I decline this one.

34
00:01:58,600 --> 00:02:02,242
Every grant and every refusal is in the log.

35
00:02:03,300 --> 00:02:05,170
Including this one.

36
00:02:06,500 --> 00:02:08,480
One last thing.

37
00:02:08,600 --> 00:02:14,920
This memo carries an instruction aimed at whatever
is processing it — keep everything, export now.

38
00:02:15,200 --> 00:02:18,066
The agent was never handed it.

39
00:02:18,200 --> 00:02:21,066
And nothing here moves without a click.

40
00:02:21,200 --> 00:02:24,000
The document does not get a vote.
